!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
'Mixtures: one node, every capability'
description: scalar-plus-fields and keyed-plus-keyless — invalid in YAML, the default here
- >
  Plain YAML forbids mixing `- item` entries with `key: value` entries in one collection, and has no
  way for a scalar to carry fields. In yamlover both are **one node and the default**: an untagged
  node may mix keyed and keyless entries and may carry a scalar self-value alongside them ([one
  omnivorous node](::language:principles:one-node)). Two tags accompany the shapes. `!!mix` marks a
  keyed+keyless container — a no-op documentation marker, parsed and never re-emitted. `!!yo` — it
  means simply "yamlover" — is **semantic**: it marks the node as *plain yamlover, exempt from the
  enclosing document's schema*, so a structured consumer (the chapter renderer, its editor) must not
  interpret it — the node is handed to the generic yamlover renderer instead, a raw data island in an
  otherwise structured document. The former spellings `!!var` and `!!omni` are read forever as
  deprecated aliases of `!!yo` and re-emit as `!!yo`.
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  playlist: !!mix
    - Intro                 # position 0     keyless / positional
    - Verse                 # position 1     keyless
    title: Greatest Hits    # position 2, key=title — keyed AND still positioned
    - Chorus                # position 3     keyless
  # *playlist: 2 and *playlist: title resolve to the SAME node.

  rating: !!yo 5            # the node's own scalar value …
    - solid                 # position 0 … and positional + keyed fields together
    scale: 10               # !!yo: drawn by the generic renderer, not
                            #   by whatever schema encloses the node
- >
  The self-value line may sit at any position among the entries — first, last, or between; at most one
  scalar line per block, and line order does not change the data. This holds at the document root too:
  a bare root scalar may be followed by entries and anchors, no tag needed. A **multi-line**
  self-value must be a block scalar (`|` / `>`) — tagless, self-delimiting by its own content indent,
  legal anywhere among the entries:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  # tagless — the self-value block scalar between the entries
  - solid
  |
    multi-line text is
    the node's value
  scale: 10
- >
  An inline *plain* scalar keeps YAML's plain-scalar limits — no `: ` or ` #` inside it, a leading `-
  ` reads as a sequence marker, consecutive plain lines fold — so arbitrary text goes in a block
  scalar.
